From 58d4bda96d12dcca974503f6953a1865775182a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:53:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Port QuickApp AI module and AI cards from staging-quickapp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Additive port of the AI stack, scoped strictly to AI surfaces:

- QuickApp AI module (src/modules/quickapp-ai): chat, AI workflows with
  the Create Agent builder, AI insights, Sahaya shell — with routes,
  Navbar entry, and the quickapp_ai module registered in the
  Security & Access Control role-permission model (fields, actions and
  widget keys identical to staging).
- Copilot chat surface (src/modules/copilot) embedded by the module's
  chat section; it calls a NEW quickapp-ai-chat edge function (staging's
  Together.ai copilot-agent under a new name) so the repo's existing
  /copilot page and its v2 copilot-agent/ai-gateway stack stay
  completely untouched.
- AI cards grafted into diverged pages without touching other logic:
  Visit Optimizer route card + per-card insight lines (MyVisits,
  VisitCard), churn risk card + row markers (MyRetailers), Beat Planner
  insights card + per-beat nudges (MyBeats, BeatCard), AI Pitch
  Suggestions with Take Action autofill (OrderEntry).
- Edge functions copied byte-identical from staging: _shared/together
  (same Together.ai endpoint and model, zero config changes),
  ai-workflow-run (+blocks/customWorkflow), ai-pitch-suggestions,
  ai-agent-builder; config.toml stanzas added.
- Migrations for ai_agents/workflow_executions (+seeds), ai_workflows,
  and the copilot conversation tables (already applied to the backing
  Supabase project).

Functions read TOGETHER_API_KEY from this project's Edge Function
secrets; until it is set, AI narration falls back deterministically.

